course: dictionary
lesson: 15694
title: Tobogganing: a winter word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Tobogganing means sliding down snowy hills on a toboggan or sledge. It names an activity, like swimming or skating: «We went tobogganing on the hill behind the school.» Read the clues around the word: snow, hill and sledge all tell you it is about sliding in winter.
explain: The -ing ending comes from the verb toboggan, and here the word names the activity. «Tobogganing is my favourite thing to do on snow days.» Your check is to swap in a simple phrase, such as "sliding on a sledge", and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Tobogganing can also be a sport. «The athletes trained all winter for the tobogganing race on the icy track.» Words like race and icy track show that this is the racing kind, not a day playing in the snow.
explain: Words can also warn you. «Always wear a helmet, and go feet first when you go tobogganing.» The safety clues show that tobogganing can be risky, so it is important to follow the rules every time.
fact: Tobogganing means sliding down snowy hills on a toboggan or sledge.
fact: Tobogganing is a noun for an activity, and it is uncountable, so we say «some tobogganing», not «a tobogganing».
fact: Tobogganing is also a winter sport of racing down icy tracks, related to luge and bobsleigh.
fact: Luge, skeleton and bobsleigh are racing kinds of tobogganing, and you can see them at the Winter Olympics.
fact: For safe tobogganing, go feet first, let one person go at a time on small hills, and keep away from roads, trees, fences and frozen ponds.
exercise: «We went tobogganing after the big snowfall.» What does tobogganing mean here? | Walking home from school | Building a snowman | *Sliding down a snowy hill on a sledge | Skating on a frozen pond
exercise: «The racers zoomed down the icy track in the tobogganing race.» What kind of activity is tobogganing here? | A kind of swimming race | A type of cooking | *A winter sport of racing on icy tracks | A summer picnic game
exercise: «Always wear a helmet and go feet first when you go tobogganing.» Find and copy one word from the sentence that is a safety clue. | *helmet | sunny | racing | summer
test: «Tobogganing down the snowy hill was the best part of our day.» What is tobogganing in this sentence? | Eating a hot lunch in the snow | *Sliding down a snowy hill on a sledge | Ice skating on a lake | Painting pictures of snow
test: «The sign said: No tobogganing near the road.» Why might there be a sign like this? | Roads are good places for racing | *Sliding near a road is dangerous | Tobogganing is quieter near roads | Snow on roads makes the hill softer
exam: «Dad took us tobogganing on the small hill and reminded us to go feet first.» What does tobogganing mean in this sentence? | Riding a bike on a road | *Sliding down a snowy hill on a sledge | Swimming in a cold lake | Painting a snowy scene
